    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Property Shop is delighted to bring this delightful bungalow with attic development to market.\r\nOnly a short walk to the Village and promenade with stunning panoramic views over lake and mountains. Superbly located in a quiet cul de sac location walking distance to lake and sea, on the edge of the Village allowing for easy access to all the local amenities. Ideally situated to take advantage of superb local amenities, golfing - Waterville Golf Club and Hogs Head Golf Course, lake and sea fishing, water sports, walking and cycling. Not to mention the many bars, restaurants and shops in the village (700m).\r\nThe property extends to circa 149 sqm or 1600 sqft and stands on a plot of 0.51 acres or 2,064 sqm. Featuring an open plan living area with two en-suite ground floor bedrooms and additional two first floor bedrooms sharing a family bathroom. There is also a generous utility room and separate w.c/cloakroom. Accommodation;- The living room features double patio doors to lake and mountain vista with a feature fireplace, a solid fuel stove/wood burner and timber ceiling, leading to a fully fitted kitchen/dining area. Bedroom 1 en-suite with picture window to lake views and a master bedroom with walk in wardrobe and en-suite. The utility room is fitted with a washing machine and dryer with generous storage and has access to w.c/cloakroom. Both first floor bedrooms have Velux windows to take in lake views and share a bathroom.\r\nOf traditional construction under a slate roof, this is a bright and airy property and is finished to a high standard. Decor is well maintained.\r\nOutside the property is approached through stone wing walls over a cattle grid and there is a shed for storage/fuel. The grounds are laid mainly to lawn with a tarmacadam driveway and generous parking and turning. The boundaries are well defined with mature hedging and fencing.\r\nAll services are connected. Featuring double glazing, gas fired central heating and septic tank system.\r\nAwaiting BER."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall: 3.64m x 1.49m - Light oak effect semi glazed front door, tiled floor, door to w.c/cloaks\r\nW.c/Cloakroom: 2m x 1.3m - Tiled floor, half tiling to walls, w.c, wash hand basin\r\nBedroom 1: 3.92m x 3.67m - En-suite, lake views\r\nEn-suite: 2.16m x 1.31m - Fully tiled, corner entry thermostatic power shower, w.c, wash hand basin\r\nLiving Room: 6.45m x 4.2m - Patio doors to lake views, tiled floor, feature fireplace with cast iron stove, open arch to kitchen/dining\r\nKitchen/Dining: 6.45m x 2.5m - Tiled floor, tiled splash backs, cherrywood light effect fitted kitchen, gas hob, bowl and a half sink, integrated appliances\r\nUtility Room: 2.6m x 3.13m - Single drainer sink, plumbed for washer/dryer, freezer, kitchen units, half glazed back door\r\nBedroom 2: 3.95m x 4.1m - En-suite, patio door to garden, walk in wardrobe\r\nWalk in Wardrobe: 1.7m x 1.5m\r\nEn-suite: 2.3m x 4.1m - Corner entry shower, Mira electric power shower, fully tiled, w.c, wash hand basin\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nBedroom 3: 4.5m x 3.7m - Lake views\r\nBathroom: 2.23m x 1.4m - Fully tiled, thermostatic power shower, w.c, wash hand basin\r\nBedroom 4: 5.25m x 4.5m - Lake views\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nShed/Store/Fuel Store: 6.2m x 1.9m"
      },
